//@version=6
// WAR FORMATION E64a — THE SHORT LEG UNDER THE SOURCE'S OWN DIRECTION RULE. 6H COLOUR IS THE GOD.
//
// USER DIRECTIVE, 2026-09-03: "my 3M and War Formation should work in both directions, not just longs
// or shorts. 6Hr is the direction for War Formation, so if red we look for shorts."
//
// THIS IS NOT A NEW IDEA — IT IS AN UNIMPLEMENTED ONE ALREADY DECODED IN ORACLE-RULES.md:
//   L204-213 "LAYER 1 — DIRECTION. The six hour is the God of direction." / "Clear direction is
//            either more than one green bar on the six hour." / "Mirrored for short."
//   L215-216 flags the deviation directly: "This is simpler and better specified than the current
//            build's 4+ green HA 1h candles inside the previous 6h block. HIS RULE IS A STRAIGHT
//            COUNT OF CONSECUTIVE 6H CANDLES."
//   L179-180 "The next build should be a single strategy that takes longs when the 6h is bullish and
//            shorts when it is bearish ... reported with both legs split out."
// Per the mandate correction, implementing a decoded-but-unimplemented source definition OUTRANKS
// inventing another short geometry. Short construction #12 — but the FIRST driven by the source's
// actual direction rule rather than by a location this lab picked.
//
// PARENT: e58a (shield $1,000 / maxBars 6480), one of the three CONFIRMED-REPRODUCIBLE builds
// (PF 1.24015239 / DD 9.82519609% / 36 trades, long). Shield and cap are held EXACTLY at e58a's
// values because HARD LESSONS 28/29 established they are coupled and both shift occupancy; changing
// either alongside the direction rule would confound this run.
//
// WHAT CHANGES, AND ONLY THIS:
//   1. Direction now comes from CONSECUTIVE 6H CANDLE COLOUR (>= 2 red), replacing the "4+ green 1H
//      candles inside the previous 6H block" proxy. This is the source's own rule.
//   2. The leg is SHORT. Mechanics are the structural mirror of the long's sweep-and-reclaim.
//
// ON LESSON 6 ("never mirror the short off the long"), STATED HONESTLY RATHER THAN WAVED PAST:
// Fourteen mirrored constructions failed, and the rule was earned. ORACLE-RULES L175-177 already
// reconciles it: "never symmetric" became "never symmetric WITHOUT SOLVING LOCATION FOR THE SHORT
// SIDE." Location IS solved here and is not assumed: the long requires brokeBelow (a 15m sweep to a
// lower low) THEN a reclaim back above it — price must have gone down and failed. The short requires
// brokeAbove (a 15m sweep to a higher high) THEN a rejection back below it — price must have gone up
// and failed. That is the same "let the enemy finish" geometry the source teaches, present on BOTH
// sides, not a naive "the regime is red so sell". E13's cycle-position gate existed precisely to bolt
// location onto a short that had none; this short has it structurally.
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) — R is the SHIELD, a fixed $1,000 dollar gap, which is the spec's own exit
//        model and a DECLARED deviation from a structural stop (ORACLE-RULES opens with it: WAR
//        FORMATION HAS NO STOP LOSS). LIVE TENSION TO WATCH: $1,000 is ~1.0% at BTC $100k but falls
//        BELOW the 0.8% floor above ~$125k. Over this window that is a real risk, not a formality.
//   Stop placement (LESSON 5) — risk-defined by the shield, not structural. Declared, per the spec.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) — SHORT ONLY here. E64b runs the long alone. Never blended.
//   BINDING (E17) — bearRegime (>= 2 consecutive red 6H) must actually bind or the direction rule is
//        inert; the trade count against e58a's 36 is the evidence and is reported either way.
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) — bearRegime and h1Bear could proxy each other (both are "price is falling").
//        They are kept because the source states BOTH ("singularity = 6h and 1h the same colour") and
//        names the 1h as a BONUS, not a requirement. If this leg produces near-zero trades, that
//        redundancy is the first suspect and h1Bear is the first term to drop — registered here in
//        advance so it is a prediction, not a post-hoc excuse.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) — the 6H colour is fixed only when the block closes; brokeAbove is
//        set on a completed 15m block; the trigger crossunder fires on a LATER 1m bar. No shared bar.
//   OCCUPANCY (LESSONS 24/28/29) — a different leg admits a genuinely different trade population, so
//        this is NOT a controlled comparison against e58a's 36 long trades. Named IN ADVANCE.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale. Position ends at target
//        or at the shield.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17):
//   * PF >= 1.0 with a usable count -> the short leg EXISTS, and fourteen prior failures were about
//     the direction rule being wrong, not about BTC having no short side. That is a major finding.
//   * PF < 1.0 -> short construction #12 fails, but for the FIRST time under the source's own
//     direction rule, which narrows the remaining space to the MECHANICS rather than the direction.
//   * near-zero trades -> bearRegime and h1Bear are redundant (see E14 above) and the next step is
//     dropping h1Bear, NOT inventing a new geometry.
//   * fewer than ~20 trades -> the ratio is a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12), and is not quoted.
strategy("War Formation E64a 6h-direction SHORT", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

run6      = input.int(2,     "Consecutive 6h candles for CLEAR DIRECTION (source: more than one)")
skipOpen  = input.int(60,    "Skip first N minutes of 6h block")
skipClose = input.int(60,    "Skip last N minutes of 6h block")
velK      = input.float(0.8, "Velocity: min rejection as multiple of atr(30)")
midLo     = input.float(400, "Whole-number middles low")
midHi     = input.float(600, "Whole-number middles high")
shieldUsd = input.float(1000,"THE SHIELD: fixed dollar gap to liquidation")
rr        = input.float(2.0, "Reward:risk")
maxBars   = input.int(6480,  "Max bars in trade -- held at e58a value")

MS6H = 21600000
MS1H = 3600000
MS15 = 900000

b6  = math.floor(time / MS6H)
b1h = math.floor(time / MS1H)
b15 = math.floor(time / MS15)

new6  = b6  != b6[1]
new1h = b1h != b1h[1]
new15 = b15 != b15[1]

var float o6   = na
var int   grn6 = 0
var int   red6 = 0

if new6
    if not na(o6)
        if close[1] > o6
            grn6 := grn6 + 1
            red6 := 0
        else if close[1] < o6
            red6 := red6 + 1
            grn6 := 0
    o6 := open

bearRegime = red6 >= run6

var float h1o = na
if new1h
    h1o := open

h1Bear = not na(h1o) and close < h1o

minsIn   = (time - b6 * MS6H) / 60000
timeGate = minsIn >= skipOpen and minsIn <= (360 - skipClose)

var float c15h = na
var float p15h = na

if new15
    p15h := c15h
    c15h := high
else
    c15h := na(c15h) ? high : math.max(c15h, high)

brokeAbove = not na(p15h) and c15h > p15h

velMin = na(ta.atr(30)) ? na : ta.atr(30) * velK

sub      = close - math.floor(close / 1000) * 1000
inMiddle = sub >= midLo and sub <= midHi

shortTrig = not na(p15h) and not na(velMin) and ta.crossunder(close, p15h) and (p15h - close) >= velMin

goShort = bearRegime and timeGate and h1Bear and brokeAbove and not inMiddle and shortTrig

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

shortR = shieldUsd

if flat and goShort and shortR > 0
    strategy.entry("S", strategy.short)
    slPx   := close + shortR
    tpPx   := close - shortR * rr
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size < 0
    strategy.exit("SX", from_entry="S", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goShort ? 1 : 0, title="ShortSignal")
plot(red6,            title="ConsecRed6h")
